      "hints": [
        "General term: $\\binom{9}{r}(2x)^{9-r}\\left(-\\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{9}{r}(-1)^r 2^{9-3r} x^{9-3r}$.",
        "Set $9 - 3r = 0 \\implies r = 3$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{9}{3}(-1)^3 2^0 = -84$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x - \\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^9$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{9}{r}(2x)^{9-r}\\left(-\\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{9}{r}2^{9-r}x^{9-r}\\left(\\frac{(-1)^r}{2^{2r}x^{2r}}\\right) = \\binom{9}{r}(-1)^r 2^{9-3r}x^{9-3r}$$",
        "To find the term independent of $x$, equate the exponent of $x$ to $0$:\n$$9 - 3r = 0 \\implies 3r = 9 \\implies r = 3$$",
        "Evaluate the constant term for $r = 3$:\n$$\\text{Term independent of } x = \\binom{9}{3}(-1)^3 2^{9-9} = 84(-1)(1) = -84$$"
      ],
